{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"494a8e733808a8f1","type":"text","text":"▶ Start","x":0,"y":0,"width":160,"height":80,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"db61e36dbc04e8ad","type":"group","label":"CLI can reach Obsidian","x":200,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"c903615036cd8a03","type":"text","text":"Verifies the Obsidian CLI can execute JavaScript in the running Obsidian instance. This is the foundation — every subsequent test depends on CLI connectivity.\n4 actions","x":250,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"040bedf1d5c3aedc","type":"group","label":"Vault accepts file operations","x":720,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"b3ebff128baf7038","type":"text","text":"Creates a test markdown file, reads it back, and verifies the content matches. Confirms the CLI-to-vault file I/O pipeline works.\n3 actions","x":770,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"b93b2a3281b6488c","type":"group","label":"Frontmatter properties persist","x":1240,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"970dea32c6540877","type":"text","text":"Creates a file with YAML frontmatter, sets a property via processFrontMatter, reads the file back and verifies the property was written.\n3 actions","x":1290,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"d65386f7a6bc3fed","type":"group","label":"Vault search indexes content","x":1760,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"076cdae085bd0f2a","type":"text","text":"Creates a file with a unique token, then verifies it is indexed by the metadata cache.\n3 actions","x":1810,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"17ace58a6f5de82d","type":"group","label":"Prepare installer state","x":2280,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"7e3c832f4894f247","type":"text","text":"In installer mode: disables plugin, resets installer state in data.json, and removes seed files via vault API. In skip mode: verifies seed files exist.\n10 actions","x":2330,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"d1fe1997ad2ea4a5","type":"group","label":"Flowti plugin activates successfully","x":2800,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"d01340c82e7e53e8","type":"text","text":"Enables the Flowti IBDE plugin, starts the EventBus event trace, and opens the Activity Log sidebar. In installer mode the wizard opens automatically; in skip mode the plugin loads normally.\n10 actions","x":2850,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"b948365b5eecca4c","type":"group","label":"Plugin reports healthy state","x":3320,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"fb9032e4e0457269","type":"text","text":"Inspects the plugin state: loaded=true, no errors, and counts the number of registered services.\n3 actions","x":3370,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"b688e67ece0ee7bb","type":"group","label":"EventBus is collecting events","x":3840,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"7f28af29c0de7afe","type":"text","text":"Verifies the plugin's EventBus is available, the E2E event trace array is initialized, and reports how many events have been collected so far.\n3 actions","x":3890,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"70e62311ea13cb21","type":"group","label":"Flowti commands are registered","x":4360,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"473c3cb0db34db18","type":"text","text":"Verifies the Flowti command pipeline is wired up by checking that the Activity Log view is present in the right sidebar.\n3 actions","x":4410,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"4a6d9a36285fade0","type":"group","label":"Required services are available","x":4880,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"64d651ed2d93d042","type":"text","text":"Reads the plugin's registered service keys, verifies the essential services are present, and writes the final summary to the progress file.\n4 actions","x":4930,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"5b5fc9c8fd04f230","type":"text","text":"⏹ End","x":5400,"y":0,"width":160,"height":80,"color":"1"}
	],
